# Officious Interrogation: two targets cost {W}{U} more (CR 601.2f), {W}{W}{U}{U} in all. With only Mox Pearl and Mox Sapphire paying, choosing both players
# leaves {W}{U} still owed after those two are spent, so the cast cannot be completed and Bot1 cancels it: the card stays in hand, nothing is on the stack and
# no Clue is made. The positive control is the sibling scenarios, where one target costs only {W}{U} and two targets are paid with {W}{W}{U}{U}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Memnite
Officious Interrogation
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Officious Interrogation.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot1; Bot2)
? Bot1.Mana = {W}{U}
Bot1.Cancel

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Hand = Officious Interrogation; Plains; Plains; Plains
Bot1.Battlefield = Memnite; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire
